Subject: [PATCH] ArmVirtPkg, OvmfPkg: PciSioSerialDxe on ArmVirtQemu, connected by BDS

Add MdeModulePkg's PciSioSerialDxe to ArmVirtQemu (DSC and FDF), so a
16550 UART behind PCI, such as QEMU's pci-serial device on virt, gets
an EFI_SERIAL_IO_PROTOCOL beside the PL011's. OvmfPkgX64 already
builds it. The console is unchanged: the platform boot manager
(PlatformBootManagerLibLight) adds only the PL011 and virtio serial
devices to ConIn, ConOut and ErrOut, so the new port is a console only
when a ConIn, ConOut or ErrOut variable names it.

PlatformBootManagerLibLight connects every device only when QEMU gives
no boot order (ConnectDevicesFromQemu fails); with a bootindex on any
device it connects just the boot devices, and the port had no
EFI_SERIAL_IO until something connected it. Its
PlatformBootManagerBeforeConsole now connects each PCI 16550 UART
(class 07h, subclass 00h, interface 02h) non-recursively, as it
connects displays, virtio input and RNG devices, so the port has its
EFI_SERIAL_IO either way. OvmfPkgX64 uses another PlatformBootManagerLib
and is not affected.

axl-firmware's patch against edk2-stable202611, applied after
0004-terminal-control-keys.patch to a copy of the packages it touches.

---
diff --git a/ArmVirtPkg/ArmVirtQemu.dsc b/ArmVirtPkg/ArmVirtQemu.dsc
index bf27866..7967906 100644
--- a/ArmVirtPkg/ArmVirtQemu.dsc
+++ b/ArmVirtPkg/ArmVirtQemu.dsc
@@ -411,6 +411,7 @@
   # PCI support
   #
   MdeModulePkg/Bus/Pci/PciHostBridgeDxe/PciHostBridgeDxe.inf
+  MdeModulePkg/Bus/Pci/PciSioSerialDxe/PciSioSerialDxe.inf
 
   #
   # Video support
diff --git a/ArmVirtPkg/ArmVirtQemuFvMain.fdf.inc b/ArmVirtPkg/ArmVirtQemuFvMain.fdf.inc
index 6379116..2fb9dd5 100644
--- a/ArmVirtPkg/ArmVirtQemuFvMain.fdf.inc
+++ b/ArmVirtPkg/ArmVirtQemuFvMain.fdf.inc
@@ -184,6 +184,7 @@ READ_LOCK_STATUS   = TRUE
   INF OvmfPkg/PciHotPlugInitDxe/PciHotPlugInit.inf
   INF OvmfPkg/VirtioPciDeviceDxe/VirtioPciDeviceDxe.inf
   INF OvmfPkg/Virtio10Dxe/Virtio10.inf
+  INF MdeModulePkg/Bus/Pci/PciSioSerialDxe/PciSioSerialDxe.inf
 
   #
   # Video support
diff --git a/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLibLight/PlatformBm.c b/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLibLight/PlatformBm.c
index 7c5fe74..5044719 100644
--- a/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLibLight/PlatformBm.c
+++ b/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLibLight/PlatformBm.c
@@ -269,6 +269,46 @@ IsPciDisplay (
   return IS_PCI_DISPLAY (&Pci);
 }
 
+/**
+  This FILTER_FUNCTION checks if a handle corresponds to a PCI 16550 UART
+  (class 07h, subclass 00h, interface 02h), such as QEMU's pci-serial.
+**/
+STATIC
+BOOLEAN
+EFIAPI
+IsPci16550 (
+  IN EFI_HANDLE    Handle,
+  IN CONST CHAR16  *ReportText
+  )
+{
+  EFI_STATUS           Status;
+  EFI_PCI_IO_PROTOCOL  *PciIo;
+  PCI_TYPE00           Pci;
+
+  Status = gBS->HandleProtocol (
+                  Handle,
+                  &gEfiPciIoProtocolGuid,
+                  (VOID **)&PciIo
+                  );
+  if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
+    return FALSE;
+  }
+
+  Status = PciIo->Pci.Read (
+                        PciIo,
+                        EfiPciIoWidthUint32,
+                        0 /* Offset */,
+                        sizeof Pci / sizeof (UINT32),
+                        &Pci
+                        );
+  if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
+    DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "%a: %s: %r\n", __func__, ReportText, Status));
+    return FALSE;
+  }
+
+  return IS_PCI_16550_SERIAL (&Pci);
+}
+
 /**
   This function checks if a handle corresponds to the Virtio Device ID given
   at the VIRTIO_DEVICE_PROTOCOL level.
@@ -1000,6 +1040,13 @@ PlatformBootManagerBeforeConsole (
   //
   FilterAndProcess (&gVirtioDeviceProtocolGuid, IsVirtioSerial, SetupVirtioSerial);
   FilterAndProcess (&gEfiPciIoProtocolGuid, IsVirtioPciSerial, SetupVirtioSerial);
+
+  //
+  // Give PCI 16550 UARTs their EFI_SERIAL_IO_PROTOCOL (PciSioSerialDxe),
+  // whether or not QEMU supplies a boot order, so that an application finds
+  // them without a full connect. They are not added to the console.
+  //
+  FilterAndProcess (&gEfiPciIoProtocolGuid, IsPci16550, Connect);
 }
 
 /**
